## Antigravity Harness Requirements Read From Reverse Engineering

Core Antigravity shape:

- Tool calls flow through converter validation, permission checks, sandbox execution, and SQLite trajectory logging (`antigravity-tool-catalogue.md:9`, `antigravity-tool-catalogue.md:32`).
- File edits use strict exact content matching and multi-hunk all-or-nothing rollback (`antigravity-tool-catalogue.md:86`, `antigravity-tool-catalogue.md:146`).
- File edit UX includes visual hunk decorations and keyboard accept/reject flow (`antigravity-tool-catalogue.md:101`, `antigravity-runtime-traces.md:104`).
- Shell execution includes persistent terminal controls, sandbox wrapper isolation, default network deny, permission prompts, and live stdout/stderr UI (`antigravity-tool-catalogue.md:303`, `antigravity-tool-catalogue.md:348`).
- Browser automation uses hermetic browser sessions, DOM/screenshot/action traces, and live visual cards (`antigravity-tool-catalogue.md:364`, `antigravity-runtime-traces.md:195`).
- Subagents create linked child trajectories and have explicit parent-child records (`antigravity-tool-catalogue.md:421`, `antigravity-runtime-traces.md:215`).
- Stop hooks evaluate diagnostics/tests and can block completion (`antigravity-runtime-traces.md:169`, `antigravity-runtime-traces.md:182`).
- Cancellation and crash recovery are first-class and DB-backed (`antigravity-runtime-traces.md:225`, `antigravity-runtime-traces.md:235`).
- Runtime persistence uses seven SQLite tables with protobuf blobs (`antigravity-protocol-schemas.md:226`, `antigravity-protocol-schemas.md:232`).
- Active session brain directory contains `implementation_plan.md`, `task.md`, `walkthrough.md`, and `scratch/` outside the workspace (`antigravity-brain-memory-architecture.md:9`, `antigravity-brain-memory-architecture.md:30`).
- Sandbox guarantees include ignored-file protection, symlink resolution, env filtering, network default deny, timeout enforcement, output limits, and browser profile isolation (`antigravity-sandbox-boundary-report.md:146`).
- Workbench UX parity P0 includes inline diff overlays, hunk navigation, causality feed, policy lease dialog, subprocess output cards, stop/resume controls, crash recovery, and diagnostics visibility (`ux/antigravity-workbench-ux-reconciliation.md:839`).

